    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0410" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/2537</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 474</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    regarding the amendment of the Regulations of the Mexican Petroleum Law,
                    necessitated by the amendment of the Law itself, which was approved by the
                    Mexican Congress in December, last, and published in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Diario Oficial</hi> of January 10, 1928, I have the honor to report that
                    the Department of Industry today handed to the representatives of the local and
                    foreign press the text of the Executive Decree signed by President Calles today
                    containing the amendments in question, together with the form to be used in
                    issuing confirmatory concessions on petroleum lands acquired prior to May 1,
                    1917. I enclose a single copy of the Spanish text of the decree in question as
                    handed to the representatives of the press by the Department of Industry today.
                    It is anticipated that this decree will appear in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Diario Oficial</hi> in the course of the next few days. Clippings from the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Diario Oficial</hi> will be sent to the Department
                    as soon as the decree appears in that publication.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d239-f1"/></p>
                <p>I also enclose an English translation of the amendments in question and of the
                    proposed form of confirmatory concession.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d239-f2"/> This
                    translation, which indicates the origin of the changes made in each case, <pb
                        facs="0411" n="301" xml:id="pg301"/> has been used by Mr. J. Reuben Clark,
                    Jr. in his negotiations on my behalf with Señor Paredes, of the Department of
                    Industry, acting on behalf of Minister Morones, and represents the substance of
                    the amendments agreed on between them.</p>
                <p>Finally, I enclose a copy of a statement handed to the press on my behalf today,
                    in connection with the amended regulations.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight W. Morrow</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d239-a1.xml" xpointer="d239-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d239-a2.xml" xpointer="d239-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
